<title>SINGAPORE: Shangri La proposes 1-for-10 bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Shangri La proposes 1-for-10 bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shangri-La Hotel Ltd said on Wednesday it was proposing a bonus issue of new shares on the basis of one new ordinary share for every 10 held.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement with its financial results for the six months to June 30, 1996, the bonus issue was designed to capitalise &quot;part of the amount standing to the credit of the company's reserves&quot;.</p>
<p>It said the bonus issue was subject to the approval of the Stock Exchange of Singapore and an extraordinary general meeting of shareholders.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
